Package: NECModel
Title: Treatment Sequencing in Small Bowel Neuroendocrine Tumours
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Thomas A.", "Trikalinos", , "ttrikalin@mac.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-3990-1848")),
    person("Yuliia", "Sereda", , "sereda_yuliia@brown.edu", role = c("aut", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4017-4561"))
    )
Description: A continuous-time microsimulation model comparing sequences of
    peptide receptor radionuclide therapy (PRRT), everolimus, and cabozantinib
    for patients with small bowel neuroendocrine tumours who progress on
    somatostatin analogues, and tools for a decision analysis under deep
    uncertainty. Transition times are drawn from non-homogeneous Poisson point
    processes; the model propagates probabilistic parameter uncertainty and
    uncertainty sets for treatment-effect attenuation and the incidence of
    post-PRRT myelodysplastic syndrome and acute myeloid leukaemia (MDS/AML)
    to mean overall survival, progression-free survival, and MDS/AML
    incidence. Treatment sequences are compared with choice functions for
    decisions under ambiguity (maximality, interval dominance, optimism,
    pessimism, Hurwicz) and summarised as Hasse diagrams.
